Maintainer: Joana da Matta <joana.damatta02@gmail.com>
Description: Provides tools for predicting intensive care unit (ICU) length of
    stay and assessing ICU efficiency with the standardized length of stay
        ('SLOS') ratio, following the methodology of Peres et al. (2022)
    <doi:10.1016/j.accpm.2022.101142> and Peres et al. (2023)
    <doi:10.1007/s00134-023-07255-w>. The package supports a pretrained model for Brazilian intensive care units, as well as a complete pipeline for building a new model from local data: feature screening and multiple imputation,
    recursive feature elimination, training of a stacked ensemble (linear
    model and random forest), and unit-level evaluation with funnel plots.
    More information: <https://github.com/igor-peres/ICU-Length-of-Stay-Prediction>.
